---
// The refusals. The one place on the site where the word tmux may appear,
// because here it names the thing Tortie protects.
---

<section class="refusals">
  <div class="container narrow">
    <h2 class="section-title">What Tortie refuses to do</h2>
    <ul class="refusal-list">
      <li>It never touches your own tmux server or your ~/.tmux.conf.</li>
      <li>It never adopts a terminal session it did not create.</li>
      <li>It never previews a key file or anything that looks like a secret.</li>
      <li>It never asks you to watch an agent work.</li>
      <li>It shows no counters and no activity feeds.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .refusals {
    padding: clamp(48px, 8vh, 88px) 0;
  }

  .refusal-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .refusal-list li {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    padding: var(--space-5) 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .refusal-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
</style>
